      en: "The Kulhudhuffushi Regional Port in the Haa Dhaalu Atoll is the primary maritime lifeline for the deep north of the Maldives. As one of the most important regional ports outside of Malé, it enables the direct import of international cargo without the need for a time-consuming detour through the capital. The facility is equipped with high-capacity cranes and expansive storage areas to efficiently handle construction materials, machinery, and food supplies. This port has drastically reduced logistics costs in the north, establishing the island hub of Kulhudhuffushi as the economic engine and main distribution center for the adjacent atolls."
