      en: "The boat building yards on Thilafushi represent a crucial industrial sector for the seafaring nation of the Maldives. A large portion of modern shipbuilding is concentrated on this reclaimed industrial island. Here, traditional Maldivian dhonis are increasingly constructed from durable fiberglass rather than wood, alongside modern yachts, transport ferries, and safari boats. The concentration of these workshops on Thilafushi pools specialized expertise, allows for economies of scale, and provides the necessary large-scale infrastructure to build and repair the vessels that form the backbone of tourism, trade, and transportation across the country."
